Kind: ablation
Issue: #709
Over: 709-widen-get-state.patch
Takes out: 17a406e9 -- thread_go() carries its own copy of the wakeup's state change again, setting TH_RUN and calling thread_setrun() whatever TH_SUSP says; over 709-widen-get-state, the receiver act_test [13] stops with thread_get_state() is put back on a run queue by the message sent to it inside the hold, runs its copyout, and the arm finds the message in its buffer before thread_get_state() has returned
Run: --entry 14 1200 -smp 4
Expect: act_test: \[13\] the receiver took a message while thread_get_state\(\) held it stopped

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/sched_prim.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/sched_prim.c
index 5c9aec6b..f6cc1c72 100644
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/sched_prim.c
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/sched_prim.c
@@ -580,10 +580,6 @@ thread_timeout_setup(
 #endif	/* NCPUS > 1 */
 }
 
-static __inline__ boolean_t	wake_dequeued(
-					thread_t	thread,
-					int		result);
-
 /*
  *	Routine:	thread_go
  *	Purpose:
@@ -639,15 +635,18 @@ thread_go(thread_t thread)
 			      thread->ith_dq_seq, thread->ith_park_seq);
 		}
 #endif	/* WAKER_TRACK */
-		/*
-		 * #709: what every wakeup does to a thread off its wait queue,
-		 * from the one copy (#607) -- and with it TH_SUSP.  A thread
-		 * that thread_stop() stopped stays off the run queues, and
-		 * thread_unstop() restarts it.  The copy that was here left
-		 * TH_SUSP out, so a message restarted a receiver while
-		 * thread_get_state() or thread_set_state() worked on it.
-		 */
-		(void) wake_dequeued(thread, THREAD_AWAKENED);
+		thread->state &= ~TH_WAIT;
+		if (!(thread->state & TH_RUN)) {
+			thread->state |= TH_RUN;
+#if	THREAD_SWAPPER
+			if (thread->state & TH_SWAPPED_OUT)
+				thread_swapin(thread->top_act, FALSE);
+			else
+#endif	/* THREAD_SWAPPER */
+				thread_setrun(thread, TRUE, TAIL_Q);
+		}
+		thread->wait_result = THREAD_AWAKENED;
+		thread->at_safe_point = NOT_AT_SAFE_POINT;
 		WAKER_NOTE(thread, THREAD_AWAKENED, NO_EVENT,
 			   __builtin_return_address(0));
 	}
